# dual_ds_dsv4 cluster config.
# Copy to `cluster.conf` and edit before running any script.
#
#   cp cluster.conf.example cluster.conf && $EDITOR cluster.conf
#
# Shared scripts/_config.sh loads this and the selected recipe. cluster.conf is .gitignored
# (it holds your site's IPs/paths) — cluster.conf.example is the committed template.

# ─── Cluster topology ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Don't know your values for a new Spark pair?  Run `bash scripts/discover.sh`
# (and `bash scripts/discover.sh <worker-ssh-addr>` to include the worker) — it
# prints ready-to-paste NODES / IFACES / TRANSFER_PEER lines.
#
# Space-separated node IPs, HEAD (rank 0, serves the API) FIRST, then workers.
# Each entry must be an IP bound to an IFACES interface on that node.  Two valid layouts:
#
#   A) Classic: the RoCE ports have IPs (e.g. 192.168.200.x / 201.x).  Put those RoCE IPs
#      here and the RoCE netdev names in IFACES; leave NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX unset.
#   B) RoCE ports WITHOUT IPs: put the management IPs here, the management NIC name in
#      IFACES (e.g. enP7s7), and set NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX=0 below.  Control traffic uses the
#      management network; tensor traffic still rides the QSFP RoCE link (~19.5 GB/s
#      all-reduce measured), and it no longer matters which QSFP port each end uses.
#
# ⚠ Do NOT use management IPs with layout A settings: with no usable RoCE GID, NCCL falls
# back to TCP sockets (~10x slower decode) or the rendezvous hangs.  00-precheck.sh checks
# that every NODES IP is on IFACES AND that each active RoCE port has a GID NCCL can use.
# This project is validated for exactly 2 DGX Sparks (TP=2); scripts generalise
# to N but >2 is untested on V4-Flash.
NODES="192.168.200.43 192.168.200.45"

# Comma-separated interface names, the SAME on every node, that carry the NODES IPs.
# Layout A: the RoCE netdevs (verify with `ibdev2netdev | awk '/Up)/{print $5}' | tr -d '()'`,
# or run scripts/discover.sh; note the UPPERCASE 'P' in `enP2p1s0f0np0`).
# Layout B: the management NIC, e.g. IFACES="enP7s7".
IFACES="enp1s0f0np0,enP2p1s0f0np0"

# Optional shared SSH key path for 00-precheck to verify is readable on every
# node.  Leave EMPTY to SKIP that check — ordinary passwordless SSH via your
# default agent/key is all the scripts actually need.  Set this only if your site
# uses a specific shared key and you want the precheck to confirm it on both nodes.
SSH_KEY=""

# RoCE GID index for NCCL's RDMA data path (layout B only; leave unset for layout A).
# 0 = RoCE v1 link-local GID derived from the port MAC: layer-2 only, needs no IPs.
# NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX=0

# ─── Container image ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Community vLLM fork built for ARM64 / sm_121 (GB10) with the DeepSeek-V4-Flash
# loader, MTP support, MLA-sparse Triton kernels, and the Marlin→DeepGEMM
# layer-42 numerical fix. This project pins that historical runtime; other builds
# require their own compatibility checks.
DOCKER_IMAGE="lmxxf/vllm-deepseek-v4-dgx-spark:marlin-fix-20260511"
CONTAINER_NAME="vllm-dsv4-mn"

# ─── Model ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HuggingFace model id.  Must be pre-downloaded on every node into
# $HF_CACHE/hub/models--deepseek-ai--DeepSeek-V4-Flash/snapshots/<hash>/.
# Use scripts/01-download-weights.sh, or `hf download $MODEL`.  ~158 GB.
MODEL="deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash"
HF_CACHE="$HOME/.cache/huggingface"

# ─── Tuning recipe ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Name (no path, no .env) of a file under config/recipes/.  Selects the operating
# point.  See Knowledge/recipes.md for the workload→recipe table.
#   interactive-128k  — default: MTP on, 131072-token configured context
#   long-output       — MTP off, 131072-token configured context
#   concurrent-32k    — MTP off, MAX_NUM_SEQS=4, 32768-token context
# interactive-200k remains a compatibility alias for interactive-128k.
# Output recommendations and historical measurements: Knowledge/performance.md.
# The `${RECIPE:-...}` form lets a one-off `RECIPE=long-output bash scripts/...`
# override this default without editing the file.
RECIPE="${RECIPE:-interactive-128k}"

# ─── Networking / ports ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NCCL rendezvous (master) port for the cross-node `mp` executor.  Non-default
# 29519 avoids ssh(22), trtllm sshd(2233), Ray(6379/8265), vLLM API(8000), and
# torch-elastic's 29400-29500 range.
HEAD_PORT=29519
# OpenAI-compatible REST port, bound on the HEAD node only.
API_PORT=8000

# ─── Safety / ops ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OOM watchdog: MemAvailable MiB below which vllm is hard-killed cluster-wide
# as a best-effort response to memory pressure.  V4-Flash needs more headroom than
# the TRT-LLM stack, so 4096 (not 2048).  See Docs/kedb/memory.md for polling limitations.
WATCHDOG_THRESHOLD_MIB=4096

# Where host-side logs (server stdout, watchdog, bench JSON) are written.
LOG_DIR="$HOME/dsv4_logs"

# Staging dir on each worker node where 03-start-serve.sh syncs run-node.sh +
# config before launching the rank there.  Persistent (survives reboot, unlike
# /tmp).  Created automatically.
REMOTE_STAGE="$HOME/dual_ds_dsv4"

# Peer address on the *201.x* subnet for 01-download-weights.sh rsync, so the
# bulk weight transfer doesn't contend with NCCL traffic on 200.x.
TRANSFER_PEER="192.168.201.45"

# Optional V4.1 EXL3 profile (see Docs/runbooks/v41.md). Keep site paths here.
# RECIPE="${RECIPE:-v41-256k}"
# V41_MODEL_DIR="$HOME/models/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-UNCENSORED-EXL3-2.9bpw"
# V41_ENGRAM_DIR="$HOME/models/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-Engram"
# V41_CACHE_DIR="$HOME/.cache/dsv41-runtime"
# V41_DOCKER_IMAGE="ghcr.io/miaai-lab/deepseek-v4.1-flash-exl3-2x-dgx-sparks@sha256:PIN"
# V41_TRANSFER_PEER="[worker-link-local-ipv6%head-qsfp-interface]"
# V41_SPEC_METHOD=none  # only enable dspark after measuring UMA headroom
# V41_IO_THREADS=32
# V41_PACKED_DIR="$HOME/models/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-Engram-packed" # run v41-service.sh pack first
